# State that is set and never taken back, and why each is right as it is: test/one_way_state.py.
# One line each, the finding, a tab, the reason. A finding with no reason here fails the check.
bit ADJ_FREQUENCY	a word of one adjtimex request, built for the call
bit AUDIO_STATE_DEVICE_ACTIVE	the state page is built whole each time it is published; the bit is that build's
bit AUDIO_STATE_OUT_HW_OFF	the state page is built whole each time it is published; the bit is that build's
bit AUDIO_STATE_OUT_HW_SET	the state page is built whole each time it is published; the bit is that build's
bit AUDIO_STATE_OUT_NO_MIXER	the state page is built whole each time it is published; the bit is that build's
bit AWK_HAS_NUMBER	a cell's state is assigned whole when its value is replaced; the bit says what the value it has is
bit AWK_HAS_TEXT	a cell's state is assigned whole when its value is replaced; the bit says what the value it has is
bit AWK_STRNUM	a cell's state is assigned whole when its value is replaced; the bit says what the value it has is
bit COLUMN_NOEXTREME	a column's properties from the command line, for the one run
bit COLUMN_ORDERED	a column's properties from the command line, for the one run
bit COMPOSITOR_XWM_OVERRIDE	what an X window is, for the record's life: state is assigned 0 when the record is given to a window (compositor_xwm_find)
bit COMPOSITOR_XWM_POPUPTYPE	what an X window is, for the record's life: state is assigned 0 when the record is given to a window (compositor_xwm_find)
bit COMPOSITOR_XWM_PROPS_READ	what an X window is, for the record's life: state is assigned 0 when the record is given to a window (compositor_xwm_find)
bit COMPOSITOR_XWM_PROTO_DELETE	protocols is assigned 0 before each WM_PROTOCOLS reply is read into it
bit COMPOSITOR_XWM_PROTO_FOCUS	protocols is assigned 0 before each WM_PROTOCOLS reply is read into it
bit COMPOSITOR_XWM_PROTO_KNOWN	what an X window is, for the record's life: state is assigned 0 when the record is given to a window (compositor_xwm_find)
bit CONVERSION_FLAG_LEFT	a flag of one parsed conversion, on the stack of its format
bit DBUS_HAS_DESTINATION	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DBUS_HAS_ERROR	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DBUS_HAS_FDS	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DBUS_HAS_INTERFACE	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DBUS_HAS_MEMBER	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DBUS_HAS_PATH	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DBUS_HAS_REPLY	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DBUS_HAS_SENDER	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DBUS_HAS_SIGNATURE	the fields one parsed message has; the message is parsed into a record of its own
bit DOC_MOD_ALT	the modifiers of one key binding as it is parsed
bit DOC_MOD_CONTROL	the modifiers of one key binding as it is parsed
bit DOC_MOD_SHIFT	the modifiers of one key binding as it is parsed
bit DOC_MOD_SUPER	the modifiers of one key binding as it is parsed
bit EDIT_HARDWARE_EIGHT	a termios word made raw; the saved word is written back whole at the end
bit EXPAND_IFS_BLANK	the table of IFS's bytes, each entry assigned whole before the bit is added
bit FORMAT_FLAG_LEFT	a flag of one parsed conversion, on the stack of its format
bit GREP_MANY_END	the automaton of one pattern set, built once for the run
bit GREP_MANY_OUT	the automaton of one pattern set, built once for the run
bit LAUNCHER_SLEEP	the word is set whole at each reading of what the kernel can do (launcher_session_read) and the bit is that reading's
bit LINK_GROUP_DONE	a one-use code that has been used: spent is where it ends, by design
bit MS_MOVE	a mount's flags from the command line, for the one call
bit MS_REMOUNT	a mount's flags from the command line, for the one call
bit PF_RANDOMIZE	the kernel's own per-task flag, set for the image being started
bit RX_ANCHORED	what a compiled pattern is, decided at compile and true for its life
bit RX_BRANCHING	what a compiled pattern is, decided at compile and true for its life
bit RX_FIRST_KNOWN	what a compiled pattern is, decided at compile and true for its life
bit RX_HAS_BACKREF	what a compiled pattern is, decided at compile and true for its life
bit RX_LAST_KNOWN	what a compiled pattern is, decided at compile and true for its life
bit RX_LITERAL_PROVES	what a compiled pattern is, decided at compile and true for its life
bit SETTINGS_ITEM_CANNOT	the list of items is zeroed and built again at each reading (settings_feed_wifi and its like)
bit SETTINGS_ITEM_DISK	the list of items is zeroed and built again at each reading (settings_feed_wifi and its like)
bit SETTINGS_ITEM_OPEN	the list of items is zeroed and built again at each reading (settings_feed_wifi and its like)
bit SETTINGS_ITEM_SAVED	the list of items is zeroed and built again at each reading (settings_feed_wifi and its like)
bit SETTINGS_ITEM_USB	the list of items is zeroed and built again at each reading (settings_feed_wifi and its like)
bit SHELL_ARRAY_ASSIGNED	what a variable is; it ends with the variable (unset)
bit SHELL_ARRAY_INDEXED	what a variable is; it ends with the variable (unset)
bit SHELL_ARRAY_READONLY	readonly cannot be taken back, by the language
bit SHELL_WAIT_DONE	a waited child's entry: done and told are where it ends, and the entry is dropped from the table
bit SHELL_WAIT_TOLD	a waited child's entry: done and told are where it ends, and the entry is dropped from the table
bit SIGNAL_KERNEL_RESTORER	a word of one sigaction request, built for the call
bit SORT_DICTIONARY	a key's ordering from the command line, for the one run
bit SORT_FOLD	a key's ordering from the command line, for the one run
bit SORT_PRINTABLE	a key's ordering from the command line, for the one run
bit SPARK_BIND_BOOT	a reply's flags, assigned 0 before they are set for the one request
bit SPARK_BIND_DEFAULT	a reply's flags, assigned 0 before they are set for the one request
bit SPARK_BIND_PENDING	a reply's flags, assigned 0 before they are set for the one request
bit SPARK_BIND_RUNNING	a reply's flags, assigned 0 before they are set for the one request
bit STREAM_MODE_KNOWN	flags is assigned whole when a stream is opened; the mode once found stays the stream's
bit TERMINAL_UL_ALTERNATIVE	ul's mode word for the one run of text it is reading
bit TERMINAL_UL_BOLD	ul's mode word for the one run of text it is reading
bit TERMINAL_UL_SUB	ul's mode word for the one run of text it is reading
bit TERMINAL_UL_SUPER	ul's mode word for the one run of text it is reading
bit TERMINAL_UL_UNDERLINE	ul's mode word for the one run of text it is reading
bit UI_BIDI_BREAK	the classes of one line being ordered, written afresh for each line
bit UI_BIDI_ISLAND	the classes of one line being ordered, written afresh for each line
bit UL_SCHED_RESET_ON_FORK	a word of one sched_setattr request, built for the call
bit UL_SCHED_UTIL_MAX	a word of one sched_setattr request, built for the call
bit UL_SCHED_UTIL_MIN	a word of one sched_setattr request, built for the call
bit WAYLAND_ICON_CONTENT	wayland.c (another hand's): what an icon object has been given, for the object's life
bit WAYLAND_ICON_SET	wayland.c (another hand's): what an icon object has been given, for the object's life
bit WAYLAND_STATE_ACTIVATED	a local copy (ask) of one configure event's facts on the stack of wayland_configure
bit WAYLAND_STATE_FULLSCREEN	a local copy (ask) of one configure event's facts on the stack of wayland_configure
bit WAYLAND_STATE_MAXIMIZED	a local copy (ask) of one configure event's facts on the stack of wayland_configure
bit WIFI_AKM_OTHER	what one heard network offers; akms is assigned before the bits are added
bit WIFI_AKM_PSK	what one heard network offers; akms is assigned before the bits are added
bit WIFI_AKM_PSK_SHA256	what one heard network offers; akms is assigned before the bits are added
bit WIFI_AKM_SAE	what one heard network offers; akms is assigned before the bits are added
bit WINDOWS_DISPLAY_OTHER	what is wrong with one display record as it is read; bad is assigned 0 first
bit WINDOWS_DISPLAY_X	what is wrong with one display record as it is read; bad is assigned 0 first
bit WINDOWS_DISPLAY_Y	what is wrong with one display record as it is read; bad is assigned 0 first
bit WINDOW_CELL_SELECTED	a cell's attributes, written with the cell each time it is drawn
bit WINDOW_CELL_WIDE	a cell's attributes, written with the cell each time it is drawn
bit WINDOW_CLOSING	the window has been asked to go, for the life of its showing: a row's state is assigned whole when its window first shows and 0 when it is let go (compositor_take, compositor_let_go); the asks are counted beside it (close_asks), and the count is what a program, the shim and the X window manager answer
bit WINDOW_NO_TAB	wayland_host.c (another hand's): a property of the row's window, cleared with the row
bit WINDOW_PLACE_SCREEN	what one placement asks, on the placement's own record
bit WINDOW_PLACE_SIZE	what one placement asks, on the placement's own record
